# Cyclopean Tomb dies (Disenchant) after putting a mire counter on Bot1's Forest and on Bot2's Island; Bot2's own Tomb put one on
# Bot1's Mountain and Tezzeret's Gambit's proliferate one more on the Forest. Then in each of Bot1's upkeeps (never Bot2's) its
# controller chooses a land this Tomb mired and no counter of it has come off: the Forest first, losing both its counters
# whoever put them there, then the Island; the Mountain was never this Tomb's, so with nothing left nothing is asked. A land is a
# Swamp only while a mire counter is on it (CR 122.1, 305.7, 603.7, 611.2b).
